  "Measured 2026-10-24 (measure.ts, evidence in measured.json): groups 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 take the photo's wall and glass colour, window shape, bay count and front class; walls[1] glass #57798f not used (not darker than the wall #79add3 by 10 L*, or tinted): kit glass kept; walls[1] curtain class not trusted (not-wall #57798f does not read as glass on #79add3 (>= 10 L* darker, chroma < 15)): brick-bay-grid kept from the building's majority; walls[1] bays and window shape not written (folded from the distrusted not-wall mask); walls[5] glass #668084 not used (not darker than the wall #82999c by 10 L*, or tinted): kit glass kept; walls[5] bays 18 from the likeness grid (padded measurement 17); walls[7] glass #728586 not used (not darker than the wall #7a9295 by 10 L*, or tinted): kit glass kept; unphotographed walls take #82999c (brick), the area-weighted median of groups 1, 2, 4, 5, 7.",
  "Cladding pass 2026-10-24 (GitHub #49, walls[].cladding): the halls are metal-clad, not brick. walls[0], [2], [3] (w01-53, w03-233, w04-143): vertical ribbed grey metal (#839192, the likeness measurement of w03-233L normalised) over a granite-concrete plinth (#8e8f89) 0.12/0.33/0.30 of the eaves tall; walls[1] (w02-323): blue horizontal profiled sheet (#79add3 measured) to the ground, a line every 0.38 m (20 across the 7.7 m crop). walls[4]-[7] (w05-233 .. w08-232): two-storey office fronts in grey-green cassette panels (the measured wall colours) about 1.3 m wide and 1.2 m tall over a granite ground with roll shutters, groups of four grey-framed windows per bay (4 bays on 19.8 m, sill 0.08 h 0.52 of the upper storey), dark roll shutters drawn as garage doors in the bays the crops show them.",
